.DS_Store

# Oracle baselines and other scratch copies of the game. One of these — a 218KB duplicate of
# index.html — got committed once because an `rm -f` ran from the wrong directory and reported success.
.tmp-*

# ⚠️ SAME HAZARD, SECOND NAMING CONVENTION, AND THE PATTERN ABOVE DID NOT COVER IT. Measuring anything
# in this game means serving a modified copy of index.html — a sweepable constant, a runtime hook, a
# build captured off HEAD — and a session that names those `.probe-*` instead of `.tmp-*` writes 500KB+
# duplicates that `.tmp-*` never sees. They were cleaned up by hand every time, which is a habit and not
# a guard: one `git add -A` before the `rm` and a stale copy of the whole game is in history for good.
#   The lesson is not "remember to delete them" — it is that a scratch-file rule keyed to ONE prefix is
# one rename away from being no rule at all. If you invent a third convention, add it here first.
.probe-*
# ...except this one, which is committed on purpose: the recorder's browser-support check, small and
# meant to be opened from a link rather than built.
!.probe-record.html

# Capacitor / npm
node_modules/
www/

# capacitor-assets insists on reading `assets/icon.png` and `assets/logo.png`, both of which are
# byte-identical copies of icons/icon-1024.png (verified by md5). Committing them would put a third
# and fourth copy of the same 433KB master in the repo and, worse, create three places to edit when
# the artwork changes. `npm run icons:ios` rebuilds the directory from the one master and regenerates.
assets/

# Recorded play. Input tapes run ~200KB of JSON per minute of play, and they are measurements rather
# than source — the harness that reads them (.harness/) IS committed.
tapes/

# Commercial planning — the free/paid split, the recommended price, the Steam page timing and the
# revenue expectations. It stays on disk and keeps being written; it is simply not part of the public
# repository. Removed from tracking rather than from history: the rest of the log stays intact, and
# every commit body that mentions it still makes sense.
docs/SCOPE.md

# Capacitor native build output. The ios/ project itself IS committed; these parts are generated.
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/App/public/
DerivedData/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/

# The key art's SOURCE candidates — several MB of generated PNGs kept for reference while choosing.
# The SHIPPED art is art/*.webp and those ARE tracked; this is the cutting-room floor. Ignored rather
# than deleted because re-deriving a crop or a colour correction needs the original, and regenerating
# it is not reproducible — the prompt is in art/KEYART-BRIEF.md but the seed is gone.
art/candidates/
